IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), Chapter 3 Part 4: sunsetting of legislative instruments (sections 50 to 54).
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
-- Same conventions as lga-register.l4: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no), NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- The days (the first 1 April or 1 October on or after the tenth anniversary, the table in section 50(2), the 24 months and the second anniversary in section 51,
-- the 5 years in section 51A(2), the list tabling day in section 52, the next sunsetting day in section 53(2)) are computed in lga-time.l4.

§ `Section 50: sunsetting`

-- Subsection (1) repeals "unless the instrument was registered on 1 January 2005": that instrument answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:889 | (1) This subsection repeals a legislative instrument on the first 1 April or 1 October falling on or after the tenth anniversary of registration of the instrument, unless the instrument was registered on 1 January 2005.
@ref s 50(1) (src:889-889)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was registered on 1 January 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1): this subsection repeals the legislative instrument on the first 1 April or 1 October on or after the tenth anniversary of its registration` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a legislative instrument` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE (IF `it was registered on 1 January 2005` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:890 | (2) This subsection repeals a legislative instrument on the day worked out using the table if the instrument was registered on 1 January 2005.
@ref s 50(2) (src:890-890)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was registered on 1 January 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(2): this subsection repeals the legislative instrument on the day worked out using the table` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a legislative instrument` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE (IF `it was registered on 1 January 2005` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- Subsection (3): section 50 has effect subject to Part 3 and sections 51, 51A, 53 and 54.
-- src:928 | (3) This section has effect subject to Part 3 (repeal of spent legislative instruments, notifiable instruments and provisions) and sections 51, 51A, 53 and 54.
-- src:929 | Note: A legislative instrument may be repealed under Part 3 before it could be repealed by this section. Section 51 or 51A may repeal a legislative instrument at a time different from the time when it would be repealed by this section. Sections 53 and 54 may prevent a legislative instrument from being repealed by this section.
@ref s 50(3) (src:928-929)
GIVEN `section 50 would repeal the legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been repealed earlier under Part 3 of this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate under section 51 or a declaration under section 51A repeals it on another day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a resolution under section 53 continues it in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 4 does not apply to it because of section 54` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(3): section 50 repeals the legislative instrument on the day it gives` MEANS
    IF NOT `section 50 would repeal the legislative instrument` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `it has been repealed earlier under Part 3 of this Chapter`
           OR `a certificate under section 51 or a declaration under section 51A repeals it on another day`
           OR `a resolution under section 53 continues it in force`
           OR `Part 4 does not apply to it because of section 54`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 51: deferral by certificate`

-- Paragraph (c) is "then ... may issue": the grant depends on (a) and (b), and where they are not met the answer is JUST FALSE ("if").
-- jural: power of the Attorney-General | liability of the legislative instrument (its sunsetting day moves)
-- src:931 | (1) If:
-- src:932 | (a) a legislative instrument would (apart from this section) be repealed by section 50 or 51A on a particular day (the sunsetting day); and
-- src:933 | (b) the Attorney-General is satisfied, on written application by the rule-maker:
-- src:934 | (i) that the instrument would (apart from the operation of this Part) be likely to cease to be in force within 24 months after the sunsetting day; or
-- src:935 | (ii) that an instrument proposed to be made in substitution for the instrument will not be able to be completed before the sunsetting day for reasons that the rule-maker could not have foreseen and avoided or because the dissolution or expiration of the House of Representatives or the prorogation of the Parliament renders it inappropriate to make a replacement instrument before a new government is formed; or
-- src:936 | (iii) that the Attorney-General has approved this Part not applying to the instrument;
-- src:937 | then:
-- src:938 | (c) the Attorney-General may issue a certificate providing that the first-mentioned instrument is repealed by this section on a 1 April or 1 October that is on or before the second anniversary of the sunsetting day and that is specified in the certificate; and
-- src:939 | (d) if the Attorney-General issues the certificate, the first-mentioned instrument is repealed by this section on the specified day instead of the sunsetting day, unless the instrument has been repealed earlier.
@ref s 51(1) (src:931-939)
GIVEN `the instrument would, apart from section 51, be repealed by section 50 or 51A on a particular day (the sunsetting day)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General is satisfied, on written application by the rule-maker, that the instrument would (apart from the operation of this Part) be likely to cease to be in force within 24 months after the sunsetting day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General is satisfied, on written application by the rule-maker, that an instrument proposed to be made in substitution will not be able to be completed before the sunsetting day for reasons the rule-maker could not have foreseen and avoided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General is satisfied, on written application by the rule-maker, that the Attorney-General has approved this Part not applying to the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(1)(c): the Attorney-General may issue a certificate providing that the instrument is repealed by section 51 on a 1 April or 1 October that is on or before the second anniversary of the sunsetting day` MEANS
    IF `the instrument would, apart from section 51, be repealed by section 50 or 51A on a particular day (the sunsetting day)`
       AND (`the Attorney-General is satisfied, on written application by the rule-maker, that the instrument would (apart from the operation of this Part) be likely to cease to be in force within 24 months after the sunsetting day`
            OR `the Attorney-General is satisfied, on written application by the rule-maker, that an instrument proposed to be made in substitution will not be able to be completed before the sunsetting day for reasons the rule-maker could not have foreseen and avoided`
            OR `the Attorney-General is satisfied, on written application by the rule-maker, that the Attorney-General has approved this Part not applying to the instrument`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 51(1)(d) (src:939-939)
GIVEN `the Attorney-General has issued the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument has been repealed earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(1)(d): the instrument is repealed by section 51 on the specified day instead of the sunsetting day` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Attorney-General has issued the certificate` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `the instrument has been repealed earlier` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:940 | (3) A certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c) is a legislative instrument.
@ref s 51(3) (src:940-940)
GIVEN `it is a certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(3): the certificate is a legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is a certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:941 | (4) Section 42 does not apply to a certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c) if the day specified in the certificate is on or before the first anniversary of the sunsetting day.
@ref s 51(4) (src:941-941)
GIVEN `it is a certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day specified in the certificate is on or before the first anniversary of the sunsetting day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(4): section 42 does not apply to the certificate` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c)` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE (IF `the day specified in the certificate is on or before the first anniversary of the sunsetting day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- jural: claim of the Parliament | duty of whoever lodges the explanatory statement for the certificate (the text does not say who)
-- src:942 | (5) The explanatory statement for a certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c) must include a statement of the reasons for the issue of the certificate.
@ref s 51(5) (src:942-942)
GIVEN `it is the explanatory statement for a certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(5): the explanatory statement must include a statement of the reasons for the issue of the certificate` MEANS
    IF `it is the explanatory statement for a certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 51A: aligning sunsetting for instruments reviewed together`

-- jural: power of the Attorney-General | liability of the instruments to be reviewed (their sunsetting day moves)
-- src:944 | (1) The Attorney-General may by legislative instrument (the sunset-altering instrument) declare that 2 or more other legislative instruments (the instruments to be reviewed) are repealed by this section on a single specified day, if he or she is satisfied, on application by the rule-maker of the instruments to be reviewed, that:
-- src:945 | (a) all the instruments to be reviewed:
-- src:946 | (i) would, apart from this section, be repealed by section 50 or 51; and
-- src:947 | (ii) are or will be the subject of a single review; and
-- src:948 | (b) the making of the declaration will facilitate the undertaking of the review or the implementation of its findings.
@ref s 51A(1) (src:944-948)
GIVEN `the number of legislative instruments to be reviewed` IS A NUMBER
      `all of them would, apart from section 51A, be repealed by section 50 or 51` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are or will be the subject of a single review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the making of the declaration will facilitate the undertaking of the review or the implementation of its findings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General is satisfied, on application by the rule-maker of the instruments to be reviewed, of those matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51A(1): the Attorney-General may by legislative instrument declare that the instruments are repealed by section 51A on a single specified day` MEANS
    IF `the number of legislative instruments to be reviewed` AT LEAST 2
       AND `all of them would, apart from section 51A, be repealed by section 50 or 51`
       AND `they are or will be the subject of a single review`
       AND `the making of the declaration will facilitate the undertaking of the review or the implementation of its findings`
       AND `the Attorney-General is satisfied, on application by the rule-maker of the instruments to be reviewed, of those matters`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:949 | (2) The day specified in the sunset-altering instrument:
-- src:950 | (a) must be 1 April or 1 October of a year; and
-- src:951 | (b) must be not more than 5 years after the earliest day on which any of the instruments to be reviewed would be repealed by section 50 or 51 apart from this section; and
-- src:952 | (c) may be the same as, or different from, any of the days on which any of the instruments to be reviewed would be repealed by section 50 or 51 apart from this section.
@ref s 51A(2) (src:949-952)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51A(2)(c): the day specified may be the same as, or different from, any of the days on which the instruments would be repealed by section 50 or 51` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:953 | (3) The sunset-altering instrument has effect according to its terms (subject to Part 2 (parliamentary scrutiny of legislative instruments), and to section 53 operating on the instruments to be reviewed).
@ref s 51A(3) (src:953-953)
GIVEN `the sunset-altering instrument is disallowed under Part 2 of this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 53 operating on the instruments to be reviewed continues them in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51A(3): the sunset-altering instrument has effect according to its terms` MEANS
    IF `the sunset-altering instrument is disallowed under Part 2 of this Chapter` OR `section 53 operating on the instruments to be reviewed continues them in force` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- jural: claim of the Parliament | duty of whoever lodges the explanatory statement for the sunset-altering instrument (the text does not say who)
-- src:954 | (4) The explanatory statement for the sunset-altering instrument must include a statement of the reasons for the making of the instrument.
@ref s 51A(4) (src:954-954)
GIVEN `it is the explanatory statement for a sunset-altering instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51A(4): the explanatory statement must include a statement of the reasons for the making of the instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is the explanatory statement for a sunset-altering instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 52: lists of instruments due for sunsetting`

-- "on each list tabling day": the duty is fixed to those days in the text's own words, so any other day answers JUST FALSE.
-- jural: claim of each House | duty of the Attorney-General
-- src:959 | (2) The Attorney-General must arrange for the laying before each House of the Parliament, on each list tabling day in relation to that House, of a list of legislative instruments that will be repealed by section 50, 51 or 51A on the sunsetting day to which that list tabling day relates.
@ref s 52(2) (src:959-959)
GIVEN `the day is a list tabling day in relation to the House` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(2): the Attorney-General must arrange for the laying before the House of a list of legislative instruments that will be repealed by section 50, 51 or 51A on the sunsetting day` MEANS
    IF `the day is a list tabling day in relation to the House` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- jural: claim of the rule-maker | duty of the Office of Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:960 | (3) As soon as practicable after the laying before either House of the Parliament of a list in accordance with subsection (2), the Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of that list to be provided to the rule-maker responsible for each legislative instrument appearing on the list.
@ref s 52(3) (src:960-960)
GIVEN `a list has been laid before either House in accordance with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislative instrument appears on the list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(3): the Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of the list to be provided to the rule-maker responsible for the legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF `a list has been laid before either House in accordance with subsection (2)` AND `the legislative instrument appears on the list` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of the rule-maker | duty of the Office of Parliamentary Counsel (limited to the earlier day)
-- src:961 | (4) If subsection (2) requires the Attorney-General to arrange for the laying of a list of the kind referred to in that subsection before the Houses of the Parliament on different days, subsection (3) need only be complied with in relation to the earlier of those days.
@ref s 52(4) (src:961-961)
GIVEN `subsection (2) requires the laying of a list before the Houses on different days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the earlier of those days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(4): subsection (3) must be complied with in relation to the day` MEANS
    IF `subsection (2) requires the laying of a list before the Houses on different days`
    THEN (IF `it is the earlier of those days` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 53: continuing an instrument in force by resolution`

-- "continues in force ... if": the conditions not met answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:963 | (1) A legislative instrument that would otherwise be repealed on a day (the repeal day) by section 50, 51 or 51A continues in force, despite those sections, if:
-- src:964 | (a) the instrument is mentioned in:
-- src:965 | (i) a copy of a certificate under section 51 that is laid before a House of the Parliament in accordance with section 38; or
-- src:966 | (ii) a list laid before a House of the Parliament under section 52; and
-- src:967 | (b) the House indicates, by resolution passed before the repeal day, that the instrument should continue in force.
@ref s 53(1) (src:963-967)
GIVEN `the instrument would otherwise be repealed on the repeal day by section 50, 51 or 51A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is mentioned in a copy of a certificate under section 51 laid before a House in accordance with section 38, or in a list laid before a House under section 52` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the House passed a resolution indicating that the instrument should continue in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `the repeal day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53(1): the legislative instrument continues in force despite sections 50, 51 and 51A` MEANS
    IF NOT `the instrument would otherwise be repealed on the repeal day by section 50, 51 or 51A` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the instrument is mentioned in a copy of a certificate under section 51 laid before a House in accordance with section 38, or in a list laid before a House under section 52`
           AND `the House passed a resolution indicating that the instrument should continue in force`
           AND NOT (`the day the resolution was passed` AT LEAST `the repeal day`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:968 | (2) The legislative instrument continues in force, subject to:
-- src:969 | (a) sections 50, 51 and 51A, which apply to it after the passage of the resolution as if it were registered on the day on which it would have been repealed by section 50, 51 or 51A apart from this section; and
-- src:970 | (b) any later instrument amending or repealing it.
-- src:971 | Note: The legislative instrument is not required to be tabled again, and is not liable to disallowance again.
@ref s 53(2) (src:968-971)
GIVEN `the legislative instrument continues in force under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a later instrument amends or repeals it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53(2)(b): the continued instrument is subject to the later instrument amending or repealing it` MEANS
    IF `the legislative instrument continues in force under subsection (1)` THEN (IF `a later instrument amends or repeals it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:971 | Note: The legislative instrument is not required to be tabled again, and is not liable to disallowance again.
@ref s 53 Note (src:971-971)
GIVEN `the legislative instrument continues in force under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53 Note: the continued instrument is required to be tabled again` MEANS
    IF `the legislative instrument continues in force under subsection (1)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 54: instruments to which Part 4 does not apply`

-- src:973 | (1) This Part does not apply in relation to a legislative instrument if the enabling legislation for the instrument (not being the Corporations Act 2001):
-- src:974 | (a) facilitates the establishment or operation of an intergovernmental body or scheme involving the Commonwealth and one or more States or Territories; and
-- src:975 | (b) authorises the instrument to be made by the body or for the purposes of the body or scheme.
@ref s 54(1) (src:973-975)
GIVEN `the enabling legislation (not being the Corporations Act 2001) facilitates the establishment or operation of an intergovernmental body or scheme involving the Commonwealth and one or more States or Territories` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enabling legislation authorises the instrument to be made by the body or for the purposes of the body or scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(1): this Part does not apply in relation to the legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF `the enabling legislation (not being the Corporations Act 2001) facilitates the establishment or operation of an intergovernmental body or scheme involving the Commonwealth and one or more States or Territories`
       AND `the enabling legislation authorises the instrument to be made by the body or for the purposes of the body or scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:976 | (2) This Part does not apply in relation to a legislative instrument if:
-- src:977 | (a) an Act provides, or has the effect, that this Part does not apply in relation to the instrument; or
-- src:978 | (b) the legislative instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of this paragraph; or
-- src:979 | (c) the legislative instrument is a regulation made for the purposes of:
-- src:980 | (i) paragraph 8(6)(b) (which covers instruments that are not legislative instruments); or
-- src:981 | (ii) paragraph 10(1)(c) (which covers instruments that are legislative instruments); or
-- src:982 | (iii) paragraph 11(2)(b) (which covers instruments that are notifiable instruments); or
-- src:983 | (iv) paragraph 44(2)(b) (which covers instruments that are not subject to disallowance); or
-- src:984 | (v) paragraph (b) of this subsection.
@ref s 54(2) (src:976-984)
GIVEN `an Act provides, or has the effect, that this Part does not apply in relation to the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislative instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 54(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislative instrument is a regulation made for the purposes of paragraph 8(6)(b), 10(1)(c), 11(2)(b), 44(2)(b) or 54(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(2): this Part does not apply in relation to the legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF `an Act provides, or has the effect, that this Part does not apply in relation to the instrument`
       OR `the legislative instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 54(2)(b)`
       OR `the legislative instrument is a regulation made for the purposes of paragraph 8(6)(b), 10(1)(c), 11(2)(b), 44(2)(b) or 54(2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:985 | (3) Prescribing a kind of instrument by regulation for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b) does not imply that every instrument of that kind is a legislative instrument.
@ref s 54(3) (src:985-985)
GIVEN `a kind of instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(3): prescribing the kind implies that every instrument of that kind is a legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF `a kind of instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
